Phoenix Configuration File, Format 0.03A


[Title]
System Shock by Origin/LookingGlass                     (Salt the Fries)

[Notes]
The System Shock Phoenix Configuration gives you access to all of the
movement and posture controls in System Shock, plus inventory, weapon,
and `ware control.  As a general rule, the joystick controls movement,
the throttle control and associated direction pad control posture
(looking up and down, leaning, crouching, crawling).  The joystick
buttons control combat functions: firing, reloading, and access to
grenades and patches.  The throttle buttons control hardwares, 
including shield, lantern, motion enhancers, nightsight, fullscreen, 
and 360 view.  The five triangular buttons on the console control your
MFD setting, and the other console buttons control other functions
likely to be used out of combat time such as mouse emulation mode and
inventory paging.

The grenade and patch interfaces deserve more explanation.  System
Shock can use a mode wherein you always have a "currently selected"
grenade and patch (highlighted in your inventory).  If you are not in
this mode, hitting either the grenade or patch button will put you in
this mode.  Otherwise, hitting the patch button will apply your
current patch.  If you do not have a grenade on your cursor, hitting
the grenade button will put your current grenade on your cursor;
otherwise the grenade on your cursor will be armed.  It can then be
thrown using the trigger like any other object. 

[Base]
Button1, Primary    {F1}  ~Left MFD slot 1
Button1, Secondary  {F6}  ~Right mfd slot 1
Button2, Primary    {F2}  ~Left MFD slot 2
Button2, Secondary  {F7}  ~Right mfd slot 2
Button3, Primary    {F3}  ~Left MFD slot 3
Button3, Secondary  {F8}  ~Right mfd slot 3
Button4, Primary    {F4}  ~Left MFD slot 4
Button4, Secondary  {F9}  ~Right mfd slot 4
Button5, Primary    {F5}  ~left MFD slot 5
Button5, Secondary  {F10}  ~Right mfd slot 5
Button6, Primary    {/}  ~mouse emulation
Button6, Secondary  {/}  ~mouse emulation
Button7, Primary    {ALT ]}  ~Inventory page ->
Button7, Secondary  {ALT [}  ~Inventory Page <-
Button8, Primary    {F}  ~Level view
Button8, Secondary  {F}  ~Level view

[Throttle/Rudder]
